From: Gork CI <gork-ci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] api-key-pure-byok: isolate explicit models and auth errors

When [auth].preferred_method is pinned to api_key, treat the process as a
pure BYOK configuration: only explicitly configured [model.*] entries are
selectable. This prevents a custom catalog alias such as `grok` routing to
`grok-4.6` from being re-resolved as the built-in `grok-4.6` entry after the
session actor stores the wire slug.

API-key sessions also have no interactive session to refresh. Keep 401/auth
failures on the API-error path instead of surfacing OAuth/WebLogin `/login`
guidance from stale auth-manager state.

Gork-Patch-Id: api-key-pure-byok
Gork-Invariant: api-key-explicit-models-only
Gork-Risk: critical
---
diff --git a/crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/config.rs b/crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/config.rs
--- a/crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/config.rs
+++ b/crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/agent/config.rs
@@ -3631,6 +3631,20 @@ pub(crate) fn resolve_model_list(
         );
         resolved.insert(key.clone(), entry);
     }
+    // A pinned API-key process is pure BYOK. Do not leave remote/built-in
+    // catalog rows around: a session stores the routing slug (`ModelInfo.model`),
+    // and a later key-first lookup could otherwise reinterpret that slug as a
+    // same-named built-in entry (for example `grok` -> `grok-4.6`).
+    if matches!(
+        cfg.grok_com_config.preferred_method,
+        Some(crate::auth::PreferredAuthMethod::ApiKey)
+    ) {
+        resolved.retain(|key, _| cfg.config_models.contains_key(key));
+        tracing::info!(
+            model_count = resolved.len(),
+            "preferred_method=api_key: using explicit [model.*] catalog only"
+        );
+    }
     for (key, entry) in resolved.iter_mut() {
         if let Some(ref mut provider) = entry.auth_provider {
             if provider.is_fail_closed() {
